experiment: aimsense
  instrument        aimsense   trial seed 0000000001358697   6 creatures
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  the question      aimfloor's 6.0 Hz used a PERFECT error signal.
                    selfcode measured what the ear actually knows
                    about the creature's own F1: 0.623 held-out
                    two-class. Does a signal THAT coarse still buy
                    error worth having?
  why it matters    it moves the bound from the PLANT to the SENSOR,
                    and it decides whether a learning rule is worth
                    building at all.
  the design        the noise level is NOT converted from 0.623. The
                    sensor is corrupted on a wide ladder and the
                    achieved accuracy is MEASURED with selfcode's own
                    statistic, so the x-axis needs no assumption.

